sn11.21:2.3 starts: What is the one thing, O Gotama,
sn11.21:2.4 starts: Whose killing you approve?”
sn11.21:3.3 starts: The killing of anger, O Vasava,
sn11.21:3.4 starts: With its poisoned root and honeyed tip:
sn11.23:2.3 starts: Goes to the terrible hell,
sn11.23:2.4 starts: Like Sambara, for a hundred years.’”
sn11.25:2.3 starts: Nonanger and harmlessness always dwell
sn11.25:2.4 starts: Within the hearts of the noble ones.
sn11.25:2.5 starts: Like a mountain avalanche
sn11.25:2.6 starts: Anger crushes evil people.’”
sn11.4:2.1 starts: “‘When face to face with Vepacitti
sn11.4:2.2 starts: Is it, Maghava, from fear or weakness
sn11.4:2.3 starts: That you endure him so patiently,
sn11.4:2.4 starts: Listening to his harsh words?’
sn11.4:4.3 starts: Hence with drastic punishment
sn11.4:4.4 starts: The wise man should restrain the fool.’
sn11.4:6.1 starts: Matali:
sn11.4:6.2 starts: In practising patient endurance:
sn11.5:9.1 starts: … verses = 877–82 …
sn11.5:9.2 none
sn11.5:10.1 none
sn11.8:4.3 starts: But for all creatures association
sn11.8:4.4 starts: Is supreme among enjoyments.
sn11.8:5.3 starts: But for all creatures association
sn11.8:5.4 starts: Is supreme among enjoyments.
sn21.10:5.2 starts: Among all things unsullied, with all cast off,
sn21.10:5.3 starts: Liberated in the destruction of craving:
